# Made by scripts/refcheck (see README.md): the full fixture corpus and baseline runs are regenerated, never
# committed. Only fixtures-mini/ and the three corpus states copied into fixtures-late/ are.
corpus/
# Baseline runs and their logs are made again from a build, and stay out. The Python baselines in
# baseline/python/ cannot be once the Python engine is gone, so they are committed (DESIGN.md
# P2.4.3).
baseline/*
!baseline/python/
# What explains each gap between the Rust runs and the Python baselines (DESIGN.md P2.4.4), which
# summarize.py --gate reads, is committed with them.
!baseline/explained.toml
